{"crc":"7a60edd0","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is that when a test dynamically adds an xfail marker using `request.node.add_marker()`, the xfail evaluation doesn't happen because `evaluate_xfail_marks()` is only called in `pytest_runtest_setup` and `pytest_runtest_call`, but the marker is added after setup has already run.\n\nThe fix should ensure that xfail marks are re-evaluated during the call phase if they weren't found during setup. Looking at the code in `skipping.py`, I can see that `pytest_runtest_call` already has logic to re-evaluate xfail marks if `xfailed` is `None`, but the issue is that `pytest_runtest_setup` always sets `xfailed_key` (even if no xfail marks are found), so the re-evaluation in `pytest_runtest_call` never triggers.\n\nThe fix is to not store `None` in `xfailed_key` when no xfail marks are found during setup, allowing the call phase to re-evaluate.\n\n# path: src/_pytest/skipping.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    if not item.config.option.runxfail:\n        item._store[xfailed_key] = xfailed = evaluate_xfail_marks(item)\n        if xfailed and not xfailed.run:\n            xfail(\"[NOTRUN] \" + xfailed.reason)\n=======\n    if not item.config.option.runxfail:\n        xfailed = evaluate_xfail_marks(item)\n        if xfailed is not None:\n            item._store[xfailed_key] = xfailed\n            if not xfailed.run:\n                xfail(\"[NOTRUN] \" + xfailed.reason)\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQVYWAG4AQJ3AMRPCAYNSYA","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQVYWABEEYYV0TJXRAZ6EY2"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786433734.4742668}
{"crc":"5dbe778b","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:d024dde6aa72446f1558de664274567cbfe347f309bc1086dd6f805ef7f1435c","instance":"01KZQVZ1TACQZA487937R6C62R","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is that when a test dynamically adds an xfail marker using `request.node.add_marker()`, the xfail evaluation doesn't happen because `evaluate_xfail_marks()` is only called in `pytest_runtest_setup` and `pytest_runtest_call`, but the marker is added after setup has already run.\n\nThe fix should ensure that xfail marks are re-evaluated during the call phase if they weren't found during setup. Looking at the code in `skipping.py`, I can see that `pytest_runtest_call` already has logic to re-evaluate xfail marks if `xfailed` is `None`, but the issue is that `pytest_runtest_setup` always sets `xfailed_key` (even if no xfail marks are found), so the re-evaluation in `pytest_runtest_call` never triggers.\n\nThe fix is to not store `None` in `xfailed_key` when no xfail marks are found during setup, allowing the call phase to re-evaluate.\n\n# path: src/_pytest/skipping.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    if not item.config.option.runxfail:\n        item._store[xfailed_key] = xfailed = evaluate_xfail_marks(item)\n        if xfailed and not xfailed.run:\n            xfail(\"[NOTRUN] \" + xfailed.reason)\n=======\n    if not item.config.option.runxfail:\n        xfailed = evaluate_xfail_marks(item)\n        if xfailed is not None:\n            item._store[xfailed_key] = xfailed\n            if not xfailed.run:\n                xfail(\"[NOTRUN] \" + xfailed.reason)\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786433734.47437}
